# Delivery envelopes are signature-bearing byte streams, not text. The
# repo-root rule (`* text=auto eol=lf`) would normalize line endings on
# commit and checkout, which changes the signed bytes: every fixture
# would fail to verify on a Windows checkout, and crlf-rewritten.envelope
# — which deliberately contains CRLF to prove a line-ending-rewriting
# transport is reported as `malformed` rather than as a mysterious
# bad-signature — would silently turn back into a valid envelope and
# stop testing anything.
#
# `-text` (not `binary`) so `git diff` still shows the readable header;
# the format is plain text precisely so it stays reviewable.
*.envelope -text
